 ],
 "intent": "Four-blade main rotor head with a swashplate flight-control stage. Power flows up the mast_shaft from the transmission: the shaft turns the hub, four blade_grips on trunnion seats carried on the hub top face, and four main_blade roots bolted to the grip outer ends. Flight control enters from below: three vertical servomechanism actuators stand on the mast_housing top face and push on the stationary swashplate ring (fixed_ring), which is deliberately non-rotating. An angular-contact thrust bearing (swash_bearing) sandwiches the fixed ring against the rotating swashplate ring (rot_ring), which is shrink-clamped to the mast so it turns and slides with it. Tilting or lifting the fixed ring tilts or lifts the rotating ring through the bearing, and four pitch_links running from the rotating ring's upper bolt circle up to the horns on each blade_grip convert that motion into blade feathering about the spanwise trunnion axes; the trunnion press fits double as the flap/feather elastomeric-equivalent hinges. The assembly is modelled at neutral pitch.",
 "units": "mm"
}